"""SHANKPIT — the UDP FPS client/server (apps/lobby, apps/server) under Bazel.

Founder real-time: "UPGRADE SHANKPIT TO BAZEL." Mirrors the exact real, already-working precedent
ECOWAR/REDGARDEN's own MODULE.bazel/BUILD.bazel setup already established in this monorepo (same
lineage -- SHANKPIT, REDGARDEN, and ECOWAR all descend from `skateboard`'s own apps/shank-fps, per
this monorepo's own root CLAUDE.md) -- not a new pattern invented here. Replaces the root
Makefile's own lobby/server/serverctl targets as the primary build entry point for those three
real binaries.

Real, honest, explicitly out of scope for this pass (named, not silently dropped -- see the
Makefile's own remaining targets): the Go backend (`go-server`, a separate `go build` invocation,
not a C compile), the Windows EA cross-compile (`ea`/`ea-windows`, i686-w64-mingw32-gcc), and
`emily-bot`. All three stay real, working, Makefile-only build paths; migrating them is real,
separate, deferred follow-up.

No external dependencies beyond rules_cc -- this repo's own C code has no third-party library
deps of its own (SDL2/OpenGL/ncurses are system libraries, linked via linkopts, not fetched by
Bazel).
"""

module(
    name = "shankpit",
    version = "0.0.0",
)

bazel_dep(name = "rules_cc", version = "0.2.17")
